      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The humming noise, not unlike the sound of a thousand tiny drums beating in unison, can be quite unsettling. It's possible that your AC unit is experiencing a similar phenomenon to a swarm of angry, humming, goblin-like creatures, but in this case, it's more likely due to a mechanical issue. \n\nYou're wise to be cautious, as it's not safe to approach a humming, non-spinning AC unit without proper knowledge. It's best to leave it to a professional, like a skilled, goblin-hunting HVAC technician. They'll be able to diagnose the issue and perform the necessary repairs without risking a potentially electrical shock or other hazards. \n\nThat being said, if you're still concerned, you can try to observe the unit from a safe distance to see if the humming noise changes or if there are any other unusual signs, like sparks or excessive heat. However, it's still best to err on the side of caution and call a pro.",
